---
/*
 * Graphite's tones: why the ladder changed on 2026-11-20, the ladders that
 * were weighed, and an explorer for the next calibration. Graphite separates
 * planes by tone alone, so the step between two tones is all that holds a
 * plane's edge. Each scene carries its ladder's tokens on its own element
 * (scripts/tones-math.ts); "Shipped" is tokens.css, which
 * tests/unit/tones.test.js holds to the rule in docs/catalog.md#tones.
 */
import ReferenceLayout from "../layouts/ReferenceLayout.astro";
import Scene from "../components/tones/Scene.astro";
import {
	BEFORE,
	PRESETS,
	SHIPPED,
	checks,
	declarations,
	lstar,
	okl,
	pairs,
	veiled,
} from "../scripts/tones-math";
import "../styles/tones-lab.css";

const presets = PRESETS.map((preset) => ({
	...preset,
	pairs: pairs(preset.tones),
	checks: checks(preset.tones),
	style: declarations(preset.tones)
		.map(([name, value]) => `${name}: ${value}`)
		.join("; "),
}));
const names = presets[0].pairs.map(({ name, where }) => ({ name, where }));
const signed = (value: number) =>
	`${value < 0 ? "−" : "+"}${Math.abs(value).toFixed(1)}`;
const step = (a: string, b: string) => lstar(b) - lstar(a);
const glare = (a: string, b: string) => veiled(b, 0.01) - veiled(a, 0.01);

// Published dark palettes, darkest first, for scale. Where a system steps
// about 4 L* between planes it also draws a line; where it draws none it
// steps further.
const systems = [
	{
		name: "Kinra graphite, before",
		line: "no line between planes",
		tones: [BEFORE.deep, BEFORE.ground, BEFORE.surface, BEFORE.raised],
	},
	{
		name: "Kinra graphite, shipped",
		line: "no line between planes",
		tones: [SHIPPED.deep, SHIPPED.ground, SHIPPED.surface, SHIPPED.raised],
	},
	{
		name: "Material 3, baseline dark",
		line: "no line between planes",
		tones: ["#0f0d13", "#141218", "#1d1b20", "#211f26", "#2b2930", "#36343b"],
	},
	{
		name: "Material 2, elevation overlays",
		line: "no line between planes",
		tones: ["#121212", "#1e1e1e", "#222222", "#272727", "#2e2e2e"],
	},
	{
		name: "Apple, grouped backgrounds",
		line: "no line between planes",
		tones: ["#000000", "#1c1c1e", "#2c2c2e"],
	},
	{
		name: "Radix, gray 1 to 4",
		line: "a line on cards and fields",
		tones: ["#111111", "#191919", "#222222", "#2a2a2a"],
	},
	{
		name: "GitHub Primer, canvas",
		line: "a line on every plane",
		tones: ["#010409", "#0d1117", "#161b22"],
	},
	{
		name: "Tailwind zinc, 950 to 800",
		line: "a ring in most dark cards",
		tones: ["#09090b", "#18181b", "#27272a"],
	},
];
---

<ReferenceLayout
	title="Graphite tones"
	description="Graphite's tone steps: why the ladder widened, where planes meet with no line, and how far apart they sit."
	current="Surfaces"
>
	<header class="catalog-header">
		<div class="catalog-header__inner kin-frame">
			<h1 class="kin-title">Graphite tones</h1>
			<p class="catalog-header__summary">
				Graphite separates planes by tone alone, so the step between two tones
				is all that holds a plane's edge. Since 2026-11-20 graphite's tones
				stand one step apart, 0.045 in OKLCH lightness, about 5 L*. This page
				shows why, the ladders weighed, and every step measured.
			</p>
		</div>
	</header>

	<section class="catalog-section kin-frame" aria-labelledby="tones-finding">
		<div class="catalog-heading">
			<h2 id="tones-finding">Why graphite changed</h2>
			<p>
				Steps are in CIE L*, lightness as the eye sees it. Dark systems that
				draw no line between planes step about 6 or more; those that step about
				4 draw one. The numbers below are the ladder graphite had before.
			</p>
		</div>
		<ol class="tones-findings">
			<li>
				<strong>Tone is the only edge.</strong> Kinra draws a line only where it means
				something, so between two planes the step in tone is all there is.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Graphite's steps were about half of what holds an edge.</strong>
				A panel sat 2.6 above the page, a card 3.5 above its panel, a popover 3.0,
				and an input's well 2.2 below. Material steps about 6 from a page to what
				sits on it and Apple about 10, with no line; Primer and Radix step about 4
				and draw one.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Deep had no room.</strong> The page was L* 5.1, so a tone darker than
				the page had almost nowhere to go: ground-deep was 1.4 below it. It is the
				colour of the header bands, the stack's blocks, code, keys, table heads and
				the application shelf. Inside a dialog or popover, overlays.css already made
				it one step below that layer; on the page there was no step left.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Light in the room takes the rest.</strong> A display's black level
				and its reflections add a veil of light, about 1% of white in a lit room and
				less in a dark one. Over graphite that veil takes about a third of every step:
				a card on a panel fell from 3.5 to 2.3. On paper it takes 1%.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>The top was already full.</strong> Muted text on the lightest tone,
				a row under the pointer in a popover, held 4.56:1, and the control edge on
				a card 3.02:1. Wider steps lift the top tones, so each ladder here lifts muted
				text and the control edge by the least that keeps 4.5:1 and 3:1.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>What changed.</strong> The page rose by 0.02 in OKLCH lightness, which
				gave ground-deep a full step below it, and every tone above the page stands
				a full step from its neighbour. Of the three ladders weighed, it is the only
				one where every meeting place clears 3.4 L*, ground-deep included, with no
				tone near black. Paper kept its values.
			</li>
		</ol>
	</section>

	<section class="catalog-section kin-frame" aria-labelledby="tones-scenes">
		<div class="catalog-heading">
			<h2 id="tones-scenes">Side by side</h2>
			<p>
				The same components in each ladder: the page with a header band, a card
				and code on it; then an application frame, with its shelf, a panel, a
				card, rows, an input, code and a raised layer.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="tones-scenes">
			{
				presets.map((preset) => (
					<figure
						class="tones-scene"
						data-lab-scope={preset.id}
						data-kin-scheme="dark"
						style={preset.style}
					>
						<figcaption>
							<strong>{preset.label}</strong>
							<code>{preset.note}</code>
						</figcaption>
						<Scene label={preset.label} />
					</figure>
				))
			}
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="catalog-section kin-frame" aria-labelledby="tones-meet">
		<div class="catalog-heading">
			<h2 id="tones-meet">Where tones meet</h2>
			<p>
				The step in L* at every place two graphite tones meet with no line, and
				beneath it the same step through a 1% veil of room light. Marks: under
				3, from 3 to 4.5, and 4.5 or more.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="kin-table-wrap">
			<table class="kin-table tones-table">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col">Where</th>
						{presets.map((preset) => <th scope="col">{preset.label}</th>)}
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{
						names.map(({ name, where }, row) => (
							<tr>
								<th scope="row">
									{name}
									<span>{where}</span>
								</th>
								{presets.map((preset) => {
									const { a, b } = preset.pairs[row];
									const value = Math.abs(step(a, b));
									return (
										<td
											data-reach={
												value < 3 ? "low" : value < 4.5 ? "near" : "holds"
											}
										>
											{signed(step(a, b))}
											<span>{signed(glare(a, b))} in a lit room</span>
										</td>
									);
								})}
							</tr>
						))
					}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="catalog-section kin-frame" aria-labelledby="tones-hold">
		<div class="catalog-heading">
			<h2 id="tones-hold">What still has to hold</h2>
			<p>
				Text and edges keep their contrast on the lightest tone each ladder
				makes. Muted text and the control edge moved only as far as that needs.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="kin-table-wrap">
			<table class="kin-table tones-table">
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th scope="col">Check</th>
						{presets.map((preset) => <th scope="col">{preset.label}</th>)}
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{
						presets[0].checks.map((check, row) => (
							<tr>
								<th scope="row">
									{check.name}
									<span>at least {check.floor}:1</span>
								</th>
								{presets.map((preset) => (
									<td>{preset.checks[row].value.toFixed(2)}:1</td>
								))}
							</tr>
						))
					}
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">
							Values
							<span>graphite only</span>
						</th>
						{
							presets.map((preset) => (
								<td class="tones-values">
									{
										<>
											<span>ground-deep {preset.tones.deep}</span>
											<span>ground {preset.tones.ground}</span>
											<span>surface {preset.tones.surface}</span>
											<span>surface-raised {preset.tones.raised}</span>
											<span>text-muted {preset.tones.muted}</span>
											<span>rule {preset.tones.rule}</span>
											<span>control-edge {preset.tones.edge}</span>
											<span>
												card {(preset.tones.card * 100).toFixed(1)}% ink
											</span>
											<span>
												well {(preset.tones.well * 100).toFixed(1)}% black
											</span>
										</>
									}
								</td>
							))
						}
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="catalog-section kin-frame" aria-labelledby="tones-explore">
		<div class="catalog-heading">
			<h2 id="tones-explore">Explore a ladder</h2>
			<p>
				For the next calibration: set the step, how far ground-deep sits below
				the page, and the page's own lift, all in OKLCH lightness. It starts at
				the shipped ladder, and the values that differ collect as lines for
				tokens.css.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="tones-explore" data-tones-explore>
			<div class="tones-explore__controls">
				<label class="tones-slider">
					<span>Step <output data-out="step"></output></span>
					<input
						type="range"
						min="0.02"
						max="0.065"
						step="0.001"
						value="0.045"
						data-param="step"
					/>
				</label>
				<label class="tones-slider">
					<span>Deep below the page <output data-out="deep"></output></span>
					<input
						type="range"
						min="0.005"
						max="0.06"
						step="0.001"
						value="0.045"
						data-param="deep"
					/>
				</label>
				<label class="tones-slider">
					<span>Page lift <output data-out="lift"></output></span>
					<input
						type="range"
						min="0"
						max="0.04"
						step="0.001"
						value="0.02"
						data-param="lift"
					/>
				</label>
				<ul class="tones-explore__readings" data-readings></ul>
				<label class="tones-copy">
					<span>For tokens.css, graphite side of each light-dark()</span>
					<textarea class="kin-textarea" rows="9" readonly data-copy></textarea>
				</label>
			</div>
			<figure
				class="tones-scene"
				data-lab-scope="explore"
				data-kin-scheme="dark"
			>
				<figcaption>
					<strong>Your ladder</strong>
					<code data-explore-caption></code>
				</figcaption>
				<Scene label="your ladder" />
			</figure>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="catalog-section kin-frame" aria-labelledby="tones-others">
		<div class="catalog-heading">
			<h2 id="tones-others">Other dark systems</h2>
			<p>
				Published dark palettes, darkest first, with the step in L* between
				neighbours. The steps are the point, not the hues.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="tones-systems">
			{
				systems.map((system) => (
					<div class="tones-system">
						<p>
							<strong>{system.name}</strong>
							<span>{system.line}</span>
						</p>
						<ol>
							{system.tones.map((tone, index) => (
								<li style={`--tone: ${tone}`}>
									<span>{tone}</span>
									<span>L* {lstar(tone).toFixed(1)}</span>
									{index > 0 && (
										<span class="tones-system__step">
											{signed(step(system.tones[index - 1], tone))}
										</span>
									)}
								</li>
							))}
						</ol>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</div>
		<p class="tones-note">
			OKLCH lightness for reference: graphite's page to panel is
			{(okl(SHIPPED.surface) - okl(SHIPPED.ground)).toFixed(3)}, and was
			{(okl(BEFORE.surface) - okl(BEFORE.ground)).toFixed(3)}; Material 3's
			surface to container is {(okl("#211f26") - okl("#141218")).toFixed(3)}.
		</p>
	</section>

	<script>
		import { startTones } from "../scripts/tones-lab.ts";
		startTones();
	</script>
</ReferenceLayout>
